th, and Australia back in sixth. The anchor leg matched " [:a {:href "/athletes/132163"} "Simone Manuel"] " for the USA, the 100 freestyle co-gold medalist, " [:a {:href "/athletes/112321"} "Cate Campbell"] " for Australia, the top female sprinter for most of the year, but one who had disappointed in Rio, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/123149"} "Pernille Blume"] " for Denmark, the 50 freestyle gold medalist. Campbell swam the fastest anchor, in 52.17, which brought Australia to the silver medal position, but they were far behind the Americans, who won gold by 1.87 seconds. Blume held on to get bronze for Denmark."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "3:54.67 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "3:53.13 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "10"} [:a {:href "/athletes/103470"} "Dana Vollmer"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/132152"} "Abbey Weitzeil"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/132154"} "Kathleen Baker"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/132155"} "Katie Meili"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/132156"} "Kelsi Worrell"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/132158"} "Lilly King"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/132162"} "Olivia Smoliga"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/132163"} "Simone Manuel"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Australia"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "3:57.80 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "3:55.00 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:cl